Overlay patch 0041: the FIRST-PERSON anchor stack (VR-spec D4,
VR-DONOR-MAP 3 "Anchor computation"). Mirrors the donor's single block at the
top of Play_Draw (z_play.c:1355-1500) almost literally, minus the hand/roomscale
pieces that belong to later rounds.

WHY IT LIVES IN Play_Draw, NOT IN THE SHELL: the anchor is a GAME quantity
(actor root, age, action state) sampled at the tick boundary, one tick per
display list, AFTER Camera_Update has run. Computing it on the compositor
thread would race the actor update and interpolate a pose against a body that
had already moved.

The five subtleties, each one of the donor's recorded scars:

1. ANCHOR = actor ROOT + eye height, NEVER actor.focus.pos (the animated head
   bone). focus.pos carries the walk-cycle bob and sway; riding it is instant
   motion sickness. The body still animates visually, the camera does not.
   (donor z_play.c:1391-1395, gVrHeadHeightOffset default -9.0.)

2. EYE HEIGHT is Player_GetHeight() (44 child / 68 adult, +32 on horse --
   z_actor.c:1401) plus that -9.0 offset. At the spec's 35 units/m that is
   1.00 m as a child and 1.69 m as an adult, which is the arithmetic that makes
   35 units/m the right world scale rather than a taste setting.

3. CRAWLING and ON_HORSE halve it (donor :1409-1424): standing height in a
   crawlspace floats the camera into the ceiling, and Link's root is already at
   the saddle. The STANDING height is exported separately so world-scale
   calibration and the child<->adult swap see a stable number.

4. +6.0 units of BODY-RELATIVE FORWARD offset, rotated by shape.rot.y (donor
   :1425-1437). Applied in game units so it interacts with world scale
   physically.

5. FAR-CAMERA FALLBACK (donor :1370-1388, gVrFpFallbackDist 1200). If the
   active camera sits further than 1200 units from Link, the first-person
   anchor is withdrawn and the shell falls back to seating on the game
   camera's own basis -- "ride the director's camera" for cutscenes framing a
   distant location, and for scenes still loading. It returns under 60% of
   that (720) so a camera hovering at the boundary cannot flap.

   NOTE (R2b scope change, the user 2026-09-03): third person is no longer a
   user-facing VR view mode -- the 3D panel mode is the third-person
   experience. This fallback is NOT that mode: it is the unnamed, automatic
   safety net spec D4 requires, and there is no setting that reaches it.

Also published here: whether first person is actually in force this tick, which
is the gate every branch of overlay 0042 reads.

rev2 (VR R3) -- THE TURN INPUT MOVED OUT OF THIS FILE ENTIRELY. rev1 ran a
snap-turn edge detector HERE, in Play_Draw, off play->state.input[0]. the user's
1.0.1.3 verdict: "when i snap turn, it stops my controller from working
properly, where i can't move anymore, and i can't perform actions, except i can
still keep snap turning."

The cause was not this detector but the input it read: LUS binds the right stick
to the C-BUTTONS as well as to right_stick_x/y
(libultraship/src/libultraship/.../ControllerDefaultMappings.cpp:94-102) at a
25% axis threshold (GlobalSDLDeviceSettings.cpp:11, MAX_AXIS_RANGE 85), so every
turn flick crossed the C threshold (21) a frame or two BEFORE it crossed the
snap threshold (51) and was still holding C when the snap disarmed. C-left /
C-right / C-up put Link into item use, first-person aiming or the ocarina --
states that eat the left stick and the face buttons -- while Play_Draw kept
running, which is precisely why turning was the only control that still worked.

The fix belongs at the ONE merged snapshot (spec D9), which is overlay 0039's
block in graph.c right after GameState_ReqPadData: see gen-patch-0039.py rev3.
rev2 of THIS patch simply deletes the detector, leaving Play_Draw to compute the
anchor and nothing else.

rev3 (VR R16 part B) -- A RETURN IS NOT AN ENTRY. the user, wearing 1.0.1.20:
"running forward, stop, pause, unpause -- it always flips me around."

The chain, and every link of it is in this tree. Overlay 0039 latches
gSohVRFlatLatch while pauseCtx.state != 0, so first person DROPS for the whole
pause -- this block is gated on the latch being 0. On unpause the latch falls,
sohVRFp goes 0 -> 1, and rev1's rising edge bumped gSohVRFpEntered
unconditionally. The shell consumes that counter as a height calibration, and
the calibration used to zero sohvr_turnYaw as well. turnYaw 0 is not "no
change": it is an ABSOLUTE compass direction -- "the wearer's forward is the
game's -Z" -- so a player running north was turned exactly 180 degrees, and
overlay 0042's facing pin then turned Link's body to match. Every far-camera
flap across the 1200/720 hysteresis did the same thing.

The yaw half of that is fixed in the shell (SohImmersive.m: the calibration
re-seats the room ORIGIN only; the yaw is reset by the explicit recenter and by
VR entry, and by nothing else). The half that belongs HERE is that those two
returns were never entries in the first place. rev3 remembers WHY first person
dropped:

  gSohVRFpEntered  -- still the RISING EDGE OF A GENUINE ENTRY: VR entry, a
                      fresh scene, first person coming up for the first time.
  gSohVRFpResumed  -- NEW: first person coming back after it was suspended by
                      something this block did to itself -- the flat latch
                      (pause, the kaleido menu, a panel room) or the far-camera
                      fallback. Counted, so `vr room` still sees every return.

Both make the shell re-seat the room origin (the wearer may genuinely have
moved during a pause); neither touches the yaw any more.

Gating: every write is inside `gSohVRMode != 0`, so the flat window, the 3D
panel and every iPhone build execute nothing but one integer test per tick.
__IOS__-only; the macOS build compiles the block with gSohVRMode a weak
constant 0.

--- a/soh/src/code/z_play.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_play.c
@@ -1349,6 +1349,108 @@
         recapturePauseBuffer = true;
     }
     // #endregion
+
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0041, VR-spec D4 / VR-DONOR-MAP 3): the first-person
+     * anchor stack. See the patch header for the five donor scars this
+     * mirrors. Runs once per tick, after Camera_Update, before the display
+     * list for this frame is built. */
+    {
+        extern volatile int gSohVRMode;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFlatLatch;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFpActive;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFpFar;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFpEntered;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFpResumed;
+        extern volatile float gSohVRFpAnchor[3];
+        extern volatile float gSohVRFpEyeHeight;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFpBodyYaw;
+        extern volatile float gSohVRHeadOffsetFwd;
+        extern volatile float gSohVRHeadHeightOffset;
+        extern volatile float gSohVRFpFallbackDist;
+        static int sSohVRFpWasActive = 0;
+        static int sSohVRFpWasFar = 0;
+        /* rev3: why first person is not in force. Set when THIS block withdrew
+         * it (flat latch or far camera), cleared the moment it is back and at
+         * every VR exit, so an entry after a suspension is counted as a resume
+         * and an entry after anything else is counted as an entry. */
+        static int sSohVRFpSuspended = 0;
+        int sohVRFp = 0;
+        if ((gSohVRMode != 0) && (gSohVRFlatLatch == 0)) {
+            Player* sohPlayer = GET_PLAYER(play);
+            Camera* sohCam = GET_ACTIVE_CAM(play);
+            if ((sohPlayer != NULL) && (sohCam != NULL)) {
+                /* (5) far-camera guard, with 0.6x hysteresis. */
+                float sohDx = sohCam->eye.x - sohPlayer->actor.world.pos.x;
+                float sohDy = sohCam->eye.y - sohPlayer->actor.world.pos.y;
+                float sohDz = sohCam->eye.z - sohPlayer->actor.world.pos.z;
+                float sohDist = sqrtf(sohDx * sohDx + sohDy * sohDy + sohDz * sohDz);
+                float sohFar = gSohVRFpFallbackDist;
+                if (sohFar < 100.0f) {
+                    sohFar = 1200.0f;
+                }
+                if (sSohVRFpWasFar) {
+                    sSohVRFpWasFar = (sohDist > (sohFar * 0.6f));
+                } else {
+                    sSohVRFpWasFar = (sohDist > sohFar);
+                }
+                if (!sSohVRFpWasFar) {
+                    /* (2)(3) eye height: standing, then the crawl/horse halving. */
+                    float sohStand = Player_GetHeight(sohPlayer) + gSohVRHeadHeightOffset;
+                    float sohEyeH = sohStand;
+                    if ((sohPlayer->stateFlags2 & PLAYER_STATE2_CRAWLING) ||
+                        (sohPlayer->stateFlags1 & PLAYER_STATE1_ON_HORSE)) {
+                        sohEyeH *= 0.5f;
+                    }
+                    /* (4) body-relative forward offset, rotated by the body yaw. */
+                    float sohYawRad = (float)sohPlayer->actor.shape.rot.y * (3.14159265358979f / 32768.0f);
+                    float sohFwdOff = gSohVRHeadOffsetFwd;
+                    /* (1) actor ROOT, never actor.focus.pos. */
+                    gSohVRFpAnchor[0] =
+                        sohPlayer->actor.world.pos.x + (sinf(sohYawRad) * sohFwdOff);
+                    gSohVRFpAnchor[1] = sohPlayer->actor.world.pos.y + sohEyeH;
+                    gSohVRFpAnchor[2] =
+                        sohPlayer->actor.world.pos.z + (cosf(sohYawRad) * sohFwdOff);
+                    gSohVRFpEyeHeight = sohStand;
+                    gSohVRFpBodyYaw = sohPlayer->actor.shape.rot.y;
+                    sohVRFp = 1;
+                }
+            }
+        } else {
+            sSohVRFpWasFar = 0;
+        }
+        gSohVRFpFar = sSohVRFpWasFar;
+        /* Recenter on the RISING edge of first person (donor :1396-1402). The
+         * shell's recenter captures nothing into steering -- that is the
+         * donor's "walking sideways" scar (VR-DONOR-MAP 4) -- so this is a
+         * pure roomscale re-seat.
+         *
+         * rev3 (VR R16 part B): AND A RETURN IS NOT AN ENTRY. The pause menu
+         * raises 0039's flat latch, which withdraws first person for the whole
+         * pause; the far-camera fallback withdraws it whenever the director's
+         * camera steps past 1200 units. Both come BACK, and rev1 counted both
+         * returns as entries -- which cost the user a 180-degree flip on every
+         * unpause while the shell still zeroed the yaw on that counter. The
+         * suspended returns get their own counter now. See the patch header. */
+        if (sohVRFp && !sSohVRFpWasActive) {
+            if (sSohVRFpSuspended) {
+                gSohVRFpResumed = gSohVRFpResumed + 1;
+            } else {
+                gSohVRFpEntered = gSohVRFpEntered + 1;
+            }
+        }
+        if (sohVRFp) {
+            sSohVRFpSuspended = 0;
+        } else if (gSohVRMode == 0) {
+            /* leaving VR is not a suspension: the next entry is a real one. */
+            sSohVRFpSuspended = 0;
+        } else if ((gSohVRFlatLatch != 0) || sSohVRFpWasFar) {
+            sSohVRFpSuspended = 1;
+        }
+        sSohVRFpWasActive = sohVRFp;
+        gSohVRFpActive = sohVRFp;
+    }
+#endif
 
     OPEN_DISPS(gfxCtx);
 
